course: dictionary
lesson: 14640
title: Precautionary: safe before harm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Precautionary» comes from «precaution», a careful step taken to stop harm before it happens. A precautionary step is one you take just in case.
explain: «The school closed the pool as a precautionary measure after the storm.» Nobody had been hurt yet. The pool was closed to keep everyone safe in case something went wrong.
explain: Look for clues. The sentence may say that nothing bad has happened yet, or that the danger may not be real. Ask: was this done to stop a problem, or after a problem had already happened? If it was before, precautionary is probably the right word.
fact: Precautionary is an adjective: it describes a noun, like «precautionary measure».
fact: «Precautionary» means done to stop something bad from happening, before it happens.
fact: In formal use, «precautionary» means done just in case, even if the danger may not be real.
fact: «A precautionary evacuation» means people leave a place to be safe, though harm may not have happened yet.
fact: Precaution is the noun, and precautionary is its adjective form.
exercise: «The town hall was evacuated as a precautionary measure when a gas smell was reported.» What does precautionary mean here? | Very slow and quiet | A kind of gas | Done after everyone was already hurt | *Done to keep people safe, just in case
exercise: Mia's mum says, «We will take a precautionary approach and check the bridge before anyone crosses.» What does a precautionary approach mean? | Ignoring the bridge | Crossing the bridge as fast as possible | Painting the bridge red | *Making safe choices early to stop harm
exercise: «The doctor sent Sam to hospital as a precautionary step, though he felt fine.» Find and copy the one word that shows the step was taken to be safe, not because of harm. | *precautionary | doctor | hospital | felt
test: «The team wore helmets as a precautionary measure on the icy hill.» What does precautionary mean? | *Done to stop harm from happening, just in case | A type of ice | Done for fun | Done after a crash
test: Nadia says precautionary means the same as careless. Is she right? | No, it means happy | *No, precautionary means careful and safe, done before harm happens | Yes, because it is a long word | Yes, both mean not careful
exam: Why would a school choose a precautionary evacuation? | *To keep everyone safe, just in case there is danger | Because the fire has already burnt the school, so it is too late to help | To make the children run around the playground | To celebrate the end of term
